.SH DESCRIPTION
The sequence retains its owner; iterators and item views do not.
Keep the storage alive, at the same address and size, and its bytes
unchanged.
A size error is yielded once, then iteration ends.
The input range has no size; each begin() scans the first item again.
Construction and iteration allocate nothing on the normal path; storage
is O(1).
Invalid ownership throws std::logic_error, or terminates without
exceptions.
Releasing the last owner can run its deleter.
